{"name":"Metroid Red","hex":"#f83800","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Metroid","blocks":[{"text":"Metroid is an action-adventure game franchise created by Nintendo. The player controls the bounty hunter Samus Aran, who protects the galaxy from Space Pirates and their attempts to harness the power of the parasitic Metroid creatures. Metroid combines the platforming of Super Mario Bros. and the exploration of The Legend of Zelda with a science fiction setting and an emphasis on nonlinear gameplay. Metroid games are mostly presented as either side-scrolling or from a first-person perspective. Players battle hostile alien enemies and obtain power-ups as they progress through the game world, with few non-player characters."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metroid","wikidata":"Q12397"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/07/NES_Metroid.png/250px-NES_Metroid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/NES_Metroid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/07/NES_Metroid.png/250px-NES_Metroid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In the original Metroid, released in 1986  for the Nintendo Entertainment System, the player controls Samus Aran, who fights aliens on the planet Zebes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANES_Metroid.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/95/Metroidprime10101.jpg/330px-Metroidprime10101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/95/Metroidprime10101.jpg/330px-Metroidprime10101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Metroid Prime, released in 2002 for the GameCube, introduced 3D graphics and first-person shooter gameplay.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMetroidprime10101.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1a/Metroid_Samus_Returns_gameplay.jpg/250px-Metroid_Samus_Returns_gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1a/Metroid_Samus_Returns_gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1a/Metroid_Samus_Returns_gameplay.jpg/250px-Metroid_Samus_Returns_gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca